<title>UK: AEA replaces Lloyds Chemists in FTSE.</title>
<headline>AEA replaces Lloyds Chemists in FTSE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist science and engineering group AEA Technology Plc, floated last year, is to replace pharmaceuticals retailer and wholesaler Lloyds Chemists in the FTSE 250 Index as of today, following the latter's acquisition by Germany's Gehe AG, FTSE International Ltd said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The decision was announced in a statement from the FTSE's actuaries UK indices committee which assesses new entrants into the main British stock indices, the FTSE 100 and the FTSE 250.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
